/-!
# Selmer modules of Galois cocycles unramified outside a set of places

Let `E` be a field (a number field in the case of interest) inside a field `Ω`, and
`G_E = Gal(Ω/E)`, the group `Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω` with the Krull topology. A *place* of `Ω` is a valuation
subring `A` of `Ω`. It lies over the finite place `v` of `E` when it contains `𝓞 E` and
`𝓞 E ∩ 𝔪_A = v`, which is `ValuationSubring.IsCenteredAt A v`. Its inertia group `I_A ≤ G_E` is
Mathlib's `ValuationSubring.inertiaSubgroup`, a subgroup of the decomposition group of `A`, read
in `G_E`. For a set `T` of finite places of `E`, `I_T ⊆ G_E`
(`TauCeti.GaloisRep.inertiaAbove E Ω T`) is the union of the `I_A` over the places `A` of `Ω` above
the places of `T`.

For a map `ρ : G_E → Mₙ(O)`, an `O`-module `B`, a set `S` of finite places of `E` and a set `L` of
relations (finitely supported functions `G_E → Mₙ(O)`), the **Selmer module** of the locally
constant `ρ`-cocycles `c : G_E → Bⁿ` unramified outside `S` and obeying `L` is
`TauCeti.cocycleSelmerModule O (n → B) ρ (inertiaAbove E Ω Sᶜ) L`, with `Mₙ(O)` acting on `Bⁿ`
through the scoped instance `Matrix.Module.matrixModule`: its members are the locally
constant `c` with `c(gh) = c(g) + ρ(g) c(h)` that vanish on the inertia groups at the places of
`Ω` over the places outside `S` and satisfy `∑_g R(g) c(g) = 0` for every `R ∈ L`. The general
theory of these modules, including functoriality in `B` and the comparison of the coefficients
`O/a` and `K/O`, is in
`TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Homological/GroupCohomology/Cocycle/SelmerModule.lean`; this file
records the properties of `I_T` and their consequences for the dependence on `S`.

For a number field `E` and `Ω = E^alg`, the places of `Ω` above `v` correspond to the maximal ideals
of the algebraic integers over `v`, and their inertia groups are those of
`TauCeti.GaloisRep.inertiaGroup`
(`TauCeti/NumberTheory/NumberField/AbsoluteGaloisGroup/ValuationSubring.lean`). For `Ω` a
separable closure, the closed subgroup generated by the inertia at the finite places outside `S`,
built from the absolute Galois groups of the completions, is
`TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.inertiaOutsideSubgroup`. The set `I_T` here is the union of the
inertia groups itself, at the places of an arbitrary extension `Ω`, which is the form in which
vanishing conditions on cocycles of an arbitrary `ρ` are stated.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.GaloisRep.inertiaAbove E Ω T`: the union `I_T` of the inertia groups at the places of
  `Ω` above the places of `T`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.GaloisRep.mem_inertiaAbove_iff`: membership in `I_T`.
* `TauCeti.GaloisRep.inertiaAbove_mono`, `TauCeti.GaloisRep.inertiaAbove_empty`,
  `TauCeti.GaloisRep.inertiaAbove_union`: `I_T` is monotone in `T`, and a union over `T`.
* `TauCeti.GaloisRep.apply_eq_zero_of_mem_cocycleSelmerModule_inertiaAbove_compl`: a member of
  the Selmer module unramified outside `S` vanishes on the inertia group of every place of `Ω`
  over a finite place outside `S`.
* `TauCeti.GaloisRep.cocycleSelmerModule_inertiaAbove_compl_mono`: enlarging `S` and dropping
  relations enlarges the Selmer module.

## References

* [J. Neukirch, *Algebraic Number Theory*][Neukirch1992], Chapter I, §9, for decomposition and
  inertia groups.

## Provenance

The set `I_T` and its name follow `New.inertiaAbove` (`src/Lib/ClassField/Local/ArtinMap.lean`)
in grh-lean (https://github.com/lsernau/grh-lean, Apache 2.0, Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC).
**Adapted, not copied**: it is stated here with Mathlib's `ValuationSubring.inertiaSubgroup` and
Tau Ceti's `ValuationSubring.IsCenteredAt`, for any field extension `Ω` of `E`.
-/

public section

open IsDedekindDomain NumberField

namespace TauCeti.GaloisRep

section InertiaAbove

variable (E Ω : Type*) [Field E] [Field Ω] [Algebra E Ω]

/-- **The inertia above a set of finite places.** For a set `T` of finite places of `E`, the union
`I_T ⊆ Gal(Ω/E)` of the inertia groups `I_A` at the places of `Ω` above the places of `T`: the
valuation subrings `A` of `Ω` that contain `𝓞 E` and meet it in a prime `v ∈ T`. -/
noncomputable def inertiaAbove (T : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E))) : Set (Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω) :=
  ⋃ v ∈ T, ⋃ (A : ValuationSubring Ω) (_ : A.IsCenteredAt v.asIdeal),
    ((A.inertiaSubgroup E).map (A.decompositionSubgroup E).subtype : Set (Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω))

variable {E Ω} {T T' : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E))} {σ : Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω}

/-- `σ` lies in `I_T` exactly when it lies in the inertia group of a place of `Ω` above a place
of `T`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_inertiaAbove_iff :
    σ ∈ inertiaAbove E Ω T ↔ ∃ v ∈ T, ∃ A : ValuationSubring Ω, A.IsCenteredAt v.asIdeal ∧
      σ ∈ (A.inertiaSubgroup E).map (A.decompositionSubgroup E).subtype := by
  simp only [inertiaAbove, Set.mem_iUnion, SetLike.mem_coe, exists_prop]

/-- The inertia group of a place of `Ω` above a place of `T` lies in `I_T`. -/
theorem map_inertiaSubgroup_subset_inertiaAbove {v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E)} (hv : v ∈ T)
    {A : ValuationSubring Ω} (hA : A.IsCenteredAt v.asIdeal) :
    ((A.inertiaSubgroup E).map (A.decompositionSubgroup E).subtype : Set (Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω)) ⊆
      inertiaAbove E Ω T :=
  fun _ hσ ↦ mem_inertiaAbove_iff.mpr ⟨v, hv, A, hA, hσ⟩

/-- `I_T` is monotone in `T`. -/
theorem inertiaAbove_mono : Monotone (inertiaAbove E Ω) :=
  fun _ _ h ↦ Set.biUnion_subset_biUnion_left h

/-- Above no places there is no inertia. -/
@[simp]
theorem inertiaAbove_empty : inertiaAbove E Ω ∅ = ∅ := by
  simp [inertiaAbove]

/-- `I_{T ∪ T'} = I_T ∪ I_{T'}`. -/
theorem inertiaAbove_union : inertiaAbove E Ω (T ∪ T') = inertiaAbove E Ω T ∪ inertiaAbove E Ω T' :=
  Set.biUnion_union T T' _

end InertiaAbove

section SelmerModule

variable {E Ω : Type*} [Field E] [Field Ω] [Algebra E Ω] {O Λ V : Type*} [CommSemiring O]
  [Semiring Λ] [Algebra O Λ] [AddCommMonoid V] [Module Λ V] [Module O V] [IsScalarTower O Λ V]
  {ρ : (Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω) → Λ} {S : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E))} {L : Set ((Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω) →₀ Λ)}

/-- **A cocycle unramified outside `S` vanishes on inertia outside `S`**: a member of the Selmer
module unramified outside `S` vanishes on the inertia group of every place of `Ω` above a finite
place `v ∉ S`. -/
theorem apply_eq_zero_of_mem_cocycleSelmerModule_inertiaAbove_compl {c : (Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω) → V}
    (hc : c ∈ cocycleSelmerModule O V ρ (inertiaAbove E Ω Sᶜ) L) {v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E)}
    (hv : v ∉ S) {A : ValuationSubring Ω} (hA : A.IsCenteredAt v.asIdeal)
    {σ : A.decompositionSubgroup E} (hσ : σ ∈ A.inertiaSubgroup E) : c σ = 0 :=
  apply_eq_zero_of_mem_cocycleSelmerModule hc
    (map_inertiaSubgroup_subset_inertiaAbove (T := Sᶜ) hv hA ⟨σ, hσ, rfl⟩)

/-- **Monotonicity in `S` and `L`**: allowing ramification at more places and dropping relations
enlarges the Selmer module. -/
theorem cocycleSelmerModule_inertiaAbove_compl_mono {S' : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E))}
    (hS : S ⊆ S') {L' : Set ((Ω ≃ₐ[E] Ω) →₀ Λ)} (hL : L' ⊆ L) :
    cocycleSelmerModule O V ρ (inertiaAbove E Ω Sᶜ) L ≤
      cocycleSelmerModule O V ρ (inertiaAbove E Ω S'ᶜ) L' :=
  cocycleSelmerModule_anti (inertiaAbove_mono (Set.compl_subset_compl.mpr hS)) hL

end SelmerModule

end TauCeti.GaloisRep
